<p local-id=3D"6938b2df7c45"><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://hel=
psystemsllc-my.sharepoint.com/:x:/g/personal/leah_guenther_helpsystems_com/=
IQAfkpPGu-u6R5cBisGm3GXMAeRD4Lvcmm9uDil_0EgZzNE" rel=3D"nofollow">Business =
Unit Changes Source of Truth</a></p>
<p local-id=3D"493d821b026d"><strong>PowerBI "Product Mapping" aka (Source =
of Truth) </strong>--&gt; <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://app.po=
werbi.com/Redirect?action=3DOpenReport&amp;appId=3Df4530bb5-b525-4717-b846-=
d1774eade730&amp;reportObjectId=3Da64d3696-aa16-43c8-91d5-f72ef195fe3d&amp;=
ctid=3Dca81e23b-3509-45ee-a998-3e346acf274d&amp;reportPage=3D1f6b4fc27f8a4a=
ee11b7&amp;pbi_source=3DappShareLink&amp;portalSessionId=3D11186844-c86d-45=
03-91b7-baee2e971981" rel=3D"nofollow"><u>Product Mapping</u></a></p>
<p local-id=3D"b9bf93a2d237"></p>
<hr local-id=3D"75fbe7e16ee8">
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"columnLayout three-equal" data-layout=3D"three-equal">
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<h1 local-id=3D"0b32a88a1ecd" id=3D"Fortra'sProductHierarchy-Salesforce">Sa=
lesforce</h1>
<h3 local-id=3D"419057a4bacf" id=3D"Fortra'sProductHierarchy-Unit0.00">Unit=
 0.00</h3>
<h3 local-id=3D"ce14d17fa2d7" id=3D"Fortra'sProductHierarchy-SolutionGroup1=
.00">Solution Group 1.00</h3>
<h3 local-id=3D"22db6fbaf378" id=3D"Fortra'sProductHierarchy-SolutionCatego=
ry2.00(AKABusinessUnit)">Solution Category 2.00 (AKA Business Unit)</h3>
<h3 local-id=3D"289dc8b67fe9" id=3D"Fortra'sProductHierarchy-Solution3.00">=
Solution 3.00</h3>
<h3 local-id=3D"950c92e3774f" id=3D"Fortra'sProductHierarchy-Sku/Product">S=
ku/Product</h3>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<h1 local-id=3D"fbca777d0bc3" id=3D"Fortra'sProductHierarchy-Workday">Workd=
ay</h1>
<h3 local-id=3D"3a88b6e6f513" id=3D"Fortra'sProductHierarchy-SuperiorOrgani=
zationSegment">Superior Organization Segment</h3>
<h3 local-id=3D"6da140de1b04" id=3D"Fortra'sProductHierarchy-FortraBusiness=
UnitHierarchy">Fortra Business Unit Hierarchy</h3>
<h3 local-id=3D"f4717581af92" id=3D"Fortra'sProductHierarchy-BusinessUnit">=
Business Unit</h3>
<h3 local-id=3D"3411454c4031" id=3D"Fortra'sProductHierarchy-Solutionleveli=
snotinWorkday"><em>Solution level is not in Workday</em></h3>
<h3 local-id=3D"7cbb8a3de316" id=3D"Fortra'sProductHierarchy-Sku/Product.1"=
>Sku/Product</h3>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<h1 local-id=3D"71f20dba8039" id=3D"Fortra'sProductHierarchy-Adaptive">Adap=
tive</h1>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"columnLayout fixed-width" data-layout=3D"fixed-width">
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<hr local-id=3D"17cd32f4b8e6">
<h1 local-id=3D"bd22f14c5d97" id=3D"Fortra'sProductHierarchy-HowisProductHi=
erarchyUsed">How is Product Hierarchy Used</h1>
<p local-id=3D"c0ce5c1a9565">Fortra Website organization (Marketing)</p>
<p local-id=3D"a3e2eaf06516">Marketing Lead association (Salesforce)</p>
<p local-id=3D"1f63323bd225">Territory Routing (Salesforce)</p>
<p local-id=3D"eb0d0913e7af">Sku Catalog Organization (Salesforce)</p>
<p local-id=3D"dabc8e678d6e">R&amp;D =E2=80=A6 Security=E2=80=A6? (Product =
Info Excel? PowerBi? Forge)</p>
<p local-id=3D"cfbfb5c1e380">PowerBi Report Filters</p>
<p local-id=3D"5776337ee355">Expense Association (Workday/concur)</p>
<p local-id=3D"db133eb65d8e">Employee Associations (Workday)</p>
<h1 local-id=3D"e6e6ec177bff" id=3D"Fortra'sProductHierarchy-SalesforceDepe=
ndencies(Fieldstoupdate,Workflows)">Salesforce Dependencies (Fields to upda=
te, Workflows)</h1>
<ul local-id=3D"a4d7bfd22989">
<li local-id=3D"e130efc84d0e">
<p local-id=3D"857f70c89b64">Marketing Products</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"77dd62806bd4">
<p local-id=3D"2aa41489b586">Territories</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0d4d57dabf6f">
<p local-id=3D"3bd8010edc9b">Price Book</p></li>
</ul>
<h1 local-id=3D"021e3befc6c5" id=3D"Fortra'sProductHierarchy-WorkdayDepende=
ncies(Fieldstoupdate,Workflows)">Workday Dependencies (Fields to update, Wo=
rkflows)</h1>
<p local-id=3D"b13a33233f1f">Superior Organization (Segment: Cyber/Tech)</p=
>
<p local-id=3D"1c978591b9f9">Fortra Business Unit Hierarchy</p>
<p local-id=3D"d27f743b93a4">Fortra Business Unit</p>
<p local-id=3D"2ce19f6ff441">SKUs &amp; Structure up to level =E2=80=9CSolu=
tion Category=E2=80=9D / =3D Business Unit</p>
<p local-id=3D"a6ebd5c1e1ac"></p>
<p local-id=3D"98a6cdb77bb5"></p>
<p local-id=3D"922ab561f27a"></p>
<p local-id=3D"687dd7f3694a">Coastal Documentation: <br></p>
<p local-id=3D"6aef3a8c40aa"><strong>Marketing Products</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"4c9368576d24">Marketing Products serve as the authoritative =
reference table for Fortra's product portfolio within Salesforce. These are=
 not standard Product objects tied to pricing or opportunity line items; ra=
ther, they are custom objects designed specifically to represent products a=
t various levels of the product hierarchy for use in territory assignment, =
product interest tracking, and campaign attribution.&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"fb00f6bd3fe5"><strong>Product Hierarchy Levels</strong>&nbsp=
;</p>
<p local-id=3D"7cd733aaba5d">Fortra's product portfolio follows a three-lev=
el hierarchy: Unit =E2=86=92 Solution Group =E2=86=92 Solution Category. Ma=
rketing Products can exist at any of these three levels, providing flexibil=
ity to define territories and track interests at the appropriate granularit=
y for different go-to-market motions.&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"bcb921a5ca3b"><strong>Unit Level:</strong> The broadest cate=
gorization, representing major product divisions such as "Tech" or "Cyber."=
 A Marketing Product at the unit level has only the Unit field populated, w=
ith Solution Group and Solution Category left blank. This level supports hi=
gh-level territory definitions and enterprise-wide product groupings.&nbsp;=
</p>
<p local-id=3D"7d75f3c621c0"><strong>Solution Group Level:</strong> A mid-l=
evel categorization representing product families within a unit, such as "R=
PA Plus" within the Tech unit or "Defensive Security" within the Cyber unit=
. Marketing Products at this level have both Unit and Solution Group popula=
ted, but Solution Category remains blank. This level provides the most comm=
on granularity for territory assignment and product interest tracking.&nbsp=
;</p>
<p local-id=3D"1844c806b197"><strong>Solution Category Level:</strong> The =
most granular level, representing specific product offerings such as "Capac=
ity Management" within RPA Plus. Marketing Products at this level have all =
three hierarchy fields populated=E2=80=94Unit, Solution Group, and Solution=
 Category. This level supports highly specialized territories and detailed =
product interest tracking.&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"e154421914d7"><strong>Marketing Product Fields</strong>&nbsp=
;</p>
<ul local-id=3D"5574cb17-5cb6-4bc3-8fbe-380bf399fb0b">
<li local-id=3D"2d2e4ced-d433-4c79-a2a5-edd456caefd1">
<p local-id=3D"b19618c9ea7d"><strong>Marketing Product Name</strong>: The d=
isplay name for the product, matching exactly what users see in the Product=
s of Interest picklist on forms, leads, and opportunities&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0e6aa270-dcff-4468-b0c7-064c827abf90">
<p local-id=3D"0deb190e6d4b"><strong>Unit</strong>: The top-level product d=
ivision (e.g., Tech, Cyber)&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"39bb77e2-3a11-466a-9072-2700f2102273">
<p local-id=3D"aa6b5d0cae1a"><strong>Solution Group</strong>: The mid-level=
 product family within the unit&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e04347d6-16f8-4e53-beed-c1035997df8d">
<p local-id=3D"4ea8b9b5bcad"><strong>Solution Category</strong>: The most g=
ranular product offering within the solution group&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a65d04c0-a08e-41ca-8d5e-606a58ce9929">
<p local-id=3D"57e9b096f5c8"><strong>Active</strong>: Checkbox indicating w=
hether this product is currently in use for assignment and tracking&nbsp;</=
p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"141d7e3432af"><strong>Active Status and Lifecycle Management=
</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"7a373e820cc5">Marketing Products can be marked as Active or =
Inactive. Active products are currently sold, marketed, and used for territ=
ory assignment. Inactive products represent deprecated offerings, sold bran=
ds, or products temporarily removed from the market.&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"241286a5b6df">When a product is deprecated, system administr=
ators set Active to false rather than deleting the Marketing Product record=
. This preserves historical relationships=E2=80=94existing Products of Inte=
rest records, territory assignments, and campaign attributions remain intac=
t, but the product no longer appears in picklists for new records or trigge=
rs new territory assignments.&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"50652c7f80fe">This lifecycle approach ensures data integrity=
 over time. Historical leads that expressed interest in a now-deprecated pr=
oduct maintain that association for reporting purposes, while new leads can=
not select the deprecated product from current picklists.&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"4d4a0f9f0dab"><strong>Synchronization with Products of Inter=
est Picklist</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"140b6e2699ef">Critical to the Marketing Products architectur=
e is the one-to-one synchronization between Marketing Product records and t=
he Products of Interest global picklist. The Products of Interest picklist =
is a global value set used on HubSpot forms, Lead records, Opportunity reco=
rds, and throughout the Salesforce environment to capture and track product=
 interests.&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"0e7ac14d80cc">Every active Marketing Product must have a cor=
responding value in the Products of Interest picklist with an exactly match=
ing name. When a prospect selects "RPA Plus" from a form dropdown, the syst=
em must be able to find a Marketing Product record named "RPA Plus" to exec=
ute territory assignment logic. If the names don't match precisely, assignm=
ent logic fails.&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"33b6ee75b3cf"><strong>Management and Maintenance</strong>&nb=
sp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"e67108820f2c">Marketing Products are managed exclusively by =
system administrators. Sales users, marketing personnel, and other end user=
s do not create, edit, or deactivate Marketing Product records. This centra=
lized control ensures data quality and prevents accidental misalignment bet=
ween Marketing Products and the Products of Interest picklist.&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"27b516deb5ba">System administrators follow a defined process=
 when introducing new products or deprecating existing ones:&nbsp;</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"0746caa6-7425-4eb6-a2b4-f6d35e9852c5">
<li local-id=3D"bc385cc1-9e7d-4a41-a1fc-cc7209edae44">
<p local-id=3D"b0191f743cb4">Create or update the Marketing Product record =
with appropriate hierarchy level and Active status&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"882547f7-c8c2-470d-914d-88dbc4489ea0">
<p local-id=3D"3f854f15dde0">Add or update the corresponding value in the P=
roducts of Interest global picklist&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c746c6b8-10de-4ef2-b72f-0500c99c567c">
<p local-id=3D"5565c62f68f3">Create or update Sales Territory records that =
reference the new/updated Marketing Product&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"10857f28-8da2-4351-b679-c95e2ad53a5a">
<p local-id=3D"698f4e990e33">Communicate changes to sales operations and ma=
rketing teams who manage forms and campaigns&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"279a89a6095c">Recommended best practice includes quarterly r=
eviews of Marketing Product records against the current product portfolio a=
nd go-to-market strategy to identify products requiring activation, deactiv=
ation, or hierarchy adjustments.&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"f3476f29188e"><strong>Usage in Territory Assignment</strong>=
&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"fa9e10457d8c">Marketing Products are not directly referenced=
 during territory assignment. Instead, Sales Territory records reference Ma=
rketing Products through their hierarchy fields (Unit, Solution Group, Solu=
tion Category). When a lead arrives with Products of Interest =3D "RPA Plus=
," the territory assignment flow searches for Sales Territory records where=
 Solution Group =3D "RPA Plus" (or Unit =3D "Tech" for broader territories)=
, then evaluates geography, industry, and named account criteria to identif=
y the matching territory.&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"cc2b74498b55">This indirect relationship provides flexibilit=
y=E2=80=94multiple Sales Territories can reference the same Marketing Produ=
ct with different coverage criteria (e.g., "RPA Plus - Northeast Geography,=
" "RPA Plus - Financial Services Industry," "RPA Plus - Named Account: Acme=
 Corp"), allowing sophisticated territory carving without requiring separat=
e Marketing Product records for each territory segment.&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"1957598caf75"><strong>Key Design Elements</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"13fb0bfc7de7"><strong>Marketing Products Object Configuratio=
n:</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<ul local-id=3D"2c0b50df-c253-4b30-b924-f69dbfd9db18">
<li local-id=3D"199479f1-0e6d-4aa3-b48e-e8f9562d41e7">
<p local-id=3D"cd65de00b1f1">Custom object serving as authoritative product=
 reference table&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4ba8d334-c7e7-4c05-8ed2-01cfe8ab1f48">
<p local-id=3D"2bbe99cdd25c">Can exist at any of three hierarchy levels: Un=
it, Solution Group, or Solution Category&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"15718721-3d59-48ce-9611-e6d5e111c09d">
<p local-id=3D"ec3322fef6e5">Unit field: Top-level product division (e.g., =
Tech, Cyber)&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cfe65125-15df-43b7-b7ea-2f43400553f4">
<p local-id=3D"d86896dd344f">Solution Group field: Mid-level product family=
 within unit&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"709dd77e-57d3-4c96-a16e-4eec3e9bf51f">
<p local-id=3D"c93163b8d9ae">Solution Category field: Most granular product=
 offering within solution group&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f5e53e07-8084-4d5b-bde6-2ecfa56e3332">
<p local-id=3D"8b1679117607">Marketing Product Name: Display name matching =
Products of Interest picklist exactly&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6853f6ea-51b6-471a-b764-9042af2f8898">
<p local-id=3D"f5d3ff02a086">Active checkbox: Indicates current use vs. dep=
recated products&nbsp;</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"7c629191c866"><strong>Data Management Requirements:</strong>=
&nbsp;</p>
<ul local-id=3D"48218a15-e040-452f-a23d-1e0bb0916670">
<li local-id=3D"50af26bc-84d9-4079-bfc0-abeed410af6b">
<p local-id=3D"69f72374db34">One-to-one synchronization required with Produ=
cts of Interest global picklist&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3543580f-2ff6-492e-a35e-8c62e1fd3ca4">
<p local-id=3D"58b3b5f9edd3">Inactive products preserve historical relation=
ships without enabling new assignments&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d1e37884-96e6-4ad9-bd15-e4fdcdfa6681">
<p local-id=3D"a47978e8df49">Managed exclusively by system administrators, =
not end users&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"55e748a4-4c56-4df3-bb75-51d74f8e1920">
<p local-id=3D"6904ab15717d">Quarterly review recommended to maintain align=
ment with product portfolio&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1d46f8b3-8384-449b-a1d9-b4af1f5de586">
<p local-id=3D"c0c63b34921c">Deletion restricted to prevent orphaned relati=
onships&nbsp;</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
